{"title":"2021 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.5</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Franklin and Giizhig travel from their school to their own homes each day. The school is located at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/7402ce2e0065c47203a152745703da0cb48793bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O(0, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"57\" height=\"20\" />. Franklin’s home is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/7/46766b6e3778b3b49e0ee518a3284ef3639e724e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F(240, 100)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" /> and Giizhig’s home is at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e15035b025e6305e84cf82780577a6a77ad4951b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G(240, 180)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"93\" height=\"20\" />. The straight paths from their school to each of their homes are shown on the graph.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(upload image on problem 2 page)\n</p><p>(Throughout this problem, all coordinates represent lengths in metres.)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the distance, in metres, along the straight path from the school to Franklin’s home?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can make a new point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/0/9c00e5249325a2b7e7bd89b5575cf0963da9d99f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X(240, 0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"20\" />, allowing us to form a right triangle to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/90583d70e91271a1ddc97f8618ddaa3fd7282422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, the distance from the school to Franklin's home.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr /> \n<p>(note: keep graph in image, just only show up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/26893d15cd5cd11ae242aeecc95704ad15a6b701.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/7/bf7f674976b7e0dbbfcbae337e348f2def8337f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 240$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" /> and don't show the other line)\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/9/4a903f7c677cbaadb6e72741b95730648ab1d442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f78904c958c7812079468105d14d93f38cba8129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$240 \\text{ m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875c1abb181a739a3ba2f3e74a6511b98ef39073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13aa51bfa913abe1acda9e7e762d4ae663390a51.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100 \\text { m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Using the pythagorean theorem, we see:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a17859d5dcaa4fe6777736e8196d64f5dda6d208.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FO^{2} = OX^{2} + FX^{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"161\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55e9516602e9ee727f21515bf09802cc7996805a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FO = \\sqrt{OX^{2} + FX^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"169\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/c/61c8adee163989ed693df5b18b7076f1ee49c9fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FO = \\sqrt{240^{2} + 100^{2}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"161\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/3/3a33b00d78572396fd74ca01128fd060366ab605.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FO = \\sqrt{57600 + 10000} = \\sqrt{676000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"277\" height=\"22\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/b/5eb7d9cbf7f27ad4e850503f1c552c3b4e896eaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed{260 \\text{ m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"79\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5\">Solution 1.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the same steps as solution 1 to form a right triangle. However, instead of using the pythagorean theorem to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/5/90583d70e91271a1ddc97f8618ddaa3fd7282422.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FO$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, we can notice that the triangle's length is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> times that of a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />-<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> triangle from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/0/450e2b42c1a53c3529df3b52b8164122859b2a31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\times 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/c/9dc54852b7c79246cd7055bea703643aaa7b3ad3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\times 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" /> being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/d/efd7f90b1c0d050ea71e884260078e17d6ffadfd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$240$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/7/007643355ed01a6d5938a6b04b3aa54644fcfbf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FO = 13 \\times 20 = \\boxed{260 \\text{ m}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"195\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018014444\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.021 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.047 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 131/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1618/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4619/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   14.102      1 -total\n 95.06%   13.405      1 2021_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_2\n 38.99%    5.499      2 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35544:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018014444 and revision id 277871. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}